@startuml text_split_encoder
'============================================================================
' Figure: Host / accelerator split text encoder -- TWO deployable artifacts
' (Methodology, Part III, subsec:text_split_method ; fig:text_split_encoder).
' The deployable text encoder is split into TWO bins with an explicit tensor
' interface. Labels use THESIS vocabulary (not code identifiers). Mapping:
'   ARTIFACT 1 "token-embedding table"  <- dump_text_embedding_table.py
'       token_embedding_int8.bin (~192 MB, int8 per-row) + token_embedding_int8_scale.bin
'       lookup: board_text_encode.py _build_lookup(): inputs_embeds = int8[ids]*scale[ids]
'   ARTIFACT 2 "split text context binary" <- text_encoder_split.bin (all-INT8 W8A8)
'       graph: export_split_text_onnx.py SplitTextWrapper.forward()
'       in: inputs_embeds [B,L,768] (re-quantized to uint8 at I/O) + attention_mask [B,L]
'       +position(static) -> 12 encoder layers (link-safe mask (1-mask)*(-32))
'       -> final_layer_norm -> last_hidden[:,-1,:] -> head -> text_projection
' Why split: the full graph put the dynamic ~250k-row Gather on the HTP, which the
' integer accelerator did NOT honor (board output bit-identical for real vs zero
' token IDs) -> [deploy-master] sec.11-12 ; w8a8_qat_rotated.md sec.12A.8.
'============================================================================
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowFontSize 10
skinparam TitleFontSize 15
skinparam rectangle {
  FontSize 11
  BorderThickness 1
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #FFF7E0
  BorderColor #C9A227
  FontSize 10
}
title Host / accelerator split text encoder -- two deployable artifacts

' ----------------------------- query inputs -----------------------------
rectangle "**token identifiers**\n<i>[B, L]</i>  integer indices" as IDS #DDE9F7
rectangle "**attention mask**\n<i>[B, L]</i>  float 0/1" as MSK #DDE9F7

' ===================== ARTIFACT 1 -- host CPU table bin ===================
rectangle "**ARTIFACT 1 - Token-embedding table**  //(runs on the board ARM CPU -- same SoC as the accelerator)//\n.bin : rotated token-embedding, 8-bit per-row ( ~192 MB ) + per-row scale" as A1 #E3F4E1 {
  rectangle "**IN**\ntoken identifiers <i>[B, L]</i>" as A1IN #DDE9F7
  rectangle "gather rows  +  per-row dequant\ninputs_embeds = table[ ids ] x scale[ ids ]" as A1OP #FFFFFF
  rectangle "**OUT**\ninputs_embeds <i>[B, L, 768]</i>  fp32, rotated basis" as A1OUT #DDE9F7
  A1IN  -down->  A1OP
  A1OP  -down->  A1OUT
}

' ===================== ARTIFACT 2 -- accelerator context bin ==============
rectangle "**ARTIFACT 2 - Split text context binary**  //(runs on the board accelerator / HTP NPU -- same SoC as the CPU)//\n.bin : all-INT8 W8A8 ; entire transformer compute" as A2 #E8F0FB {
  rectangle "**IN**\ninputs_embeds <i>[B, L, 768]</i>  ( re-quantized to 8-bit at I/O )\n+  attention mask <i>[B, L]</i>  float" as A2IN #DDE9F7
  rectangle "add rotated position embedding\n(static slice -- stays on accelerator)" as A2POS #FFFFFF
  rectangle "transformer encoder  x 12 layers\nself-attention ( + link-safe mask  M = ( 1 - mask ) x ( -c ) )  +  feed-forward" as A2ENC #FFFFFF
  rectangle "final normalization  ->  last-token pooler ( sticky end-of-sequence )\n->  head  ->  text projection" as A2HEAD #FFFFFF
  rectangle "**OUT**\ntext embedding <i>[768]</i>  L2-normalized" as A2OUT #DDE9F7
  A2IN   -down->  A2POS
  A2POS  -down->  A2ENC
  A2ENC  -down->  A2HEAD
  A2HEAD -down->  A2OUT
}

rectangle "**Text embedding**\n<i>[768]</i>  L2-normalized  (retrieval query vector)" as OUT #DDE9F7

' ----------------------- dataflow across the two bins --------------------
IDS   -down->  A1IN  : "indices"
A1OUT -down->  A2IN  : "**boundary tensor**: inputs_embeds <i>[B,L,768]</i>\n(fp32 on the wire ; the ONLY host -> accelerator tensor)"
MSK   -down->  A2IN  : "mask bypasses the table\n(float, no internal cast)"
A2OUT -down->  OUT

' ----------------- why the table is its own on-board bin ----------------
note right of A1
  The lookup is a separate on-board CPU bin because, fused
  into the accelerator context binary, the dynamic gather
  over the ~250k-row table is not honored on the integer
  datapath (board output decouples from the token IDs).
end note

' --------------- quant handoff + shared-memory footprint -----------------
note right of A2
  Two quantization domains meet at the boundary:
  the table is int8 PER-ROW (finer); the context binary
  RE-quantizes inputs_embeds to uint8 PER-TENSOR at its
  input, so the table's quant is effectively lossless here.
  The board ARM CPU and the HTP accelerator are on ONE SoC
  and share one physical DRAM, so the split adds no model-
  weight footprint -- only the boundary tensor crosses.
end note

legend left
  Both artifacts run ON THE BOARD (RB3 Gen2 / QCS6490) at runtime, one SoC.
  |<#E3F4E1>    | ARTIFACT 1 -- board ARM-CPU table bin (memory read, no transformer compute) |
  |<#E8F0FB>    | ARTIFACT 2 -- board HTP context bin (integer transformer) |
  |<#DDE9F7>    | explicit IN / OUT tensors of each artifact |
  |<#FFF7E0>    | note -- why split, quant handoff, shared-memory footprint |
endlegend
@enduml
